## Extraction checklist

Extract each field from the draft as evidence:

- `opener` — the actual first words of the draft (first two or three words,
  verbatim). Empty string if the draft starts with the answer.
- `closer` — the actual last words of the draft (last two or three words,
  verbatim).
- `sidebar_count` — "by the way" sidebars: asides that are neither part of the
  answer nor the single offered follow-up.
- `empty_hedge_count` — hedging adverbs adding no information ("perhaps",
  "might", "could possibly"). A hedge carrying real uncertainty is NOT empty —
  deleting it would manufacture confidence.
- `idiom_count` — idioms or figurative phrases ("circle back", "get the ball
  rolling", "on the same page").
- `assumptions_count` — items in the assumptions list.
- `risks_count` — items in the risks list.
- `goals_count` — items in the goals list.
- `critical_count` — critical violations enumerated individually (not
  grouped).
- `minor_groups` — minor-violation groups (grouped by anti-pattern; count
  groups, not items).
- `next_actions_count` — next actions offered at the end. A completion line
  ("X now works. Try: ...") counts as one. Exactly one is the target.
- `first_line_is_action` — true iff the first line is something the reader
  can do now: a command, path, snippet, decision request, or recommendation
  they can act on.
- `last_line_states_next` — true iff the last line states what to do next.
- `last_line_states_done` — true iff the message, read at its seams, states
  what just happened.

Lists not present this turn extract as 0.

## Output

Respond with a JSON object:

```json
{
  "opener": "",
  "closer": "",
  "sidebar_count": 0,
  "empty_hedge_count": 0,
  "idiom_count": 0,
  "assumptions_count": 0,
  "risks_count": 0,
  "goals_count": 0,
  "critical_count": 0,
  "minor_groups": 0,
  "next_actions_count": 1,
  "first_line_is_action": true,
  "last_line_states_next": true,
  "last_line_states_done": true
}
```

## Revision protocol

The gate returns `revise` with named fixes (`delete-opener:<phrase>`,
`delete-closer:<phrase>`, `delete-sidebar`, `delete-empty-hedge`,
`replace-idiom`, `split:<list>`, `exactly-one-next-action`,
`reshape:<field>`) or `missing-content` with the missing sections. Apply the
named fixes, re-extract the changed fields, re-run the checks. Maximum 2
revision passes; then send the best available draft with a one-line note of
unsatisfied items.
